// fixed-position cameras (autoscrolls and scripted holds via SetAutoScrollPos; camera controller 0x006C5970, target at
// 0x006C6FD0): keep the fixed Y/Z. While the fixed X moves the camera rides it exactly like stock; once it has been still
// for 2 s (stopped or vertical scroll) X may follow the camera focus within fixed X +/- the reach delta, so the 4:3 view
// pans inside the 16:9 frame. Room changes start on the game's position (cave G at 0x02138A00, generated below).
// StopScroll side locks (e.g. the Wonder shaft in Up 'n' Down with Puffy Lifts): the locked camera X may pan by the
// area's reach delta (cave H at 0x02138F00, hook 0x006C7BEC); boss rooms in the table use delta 0 = stock lock.
// Per-area view zoom (generator: tools/gen_zoom_v2.py, v2). The base view height G of the current area is
// written to a spare word at 0x037D1F00 by cave A and read by the view, camera-clamp and pipe-box hooks:
//   boss arenas (area hashes in the table at 02138E00): Course150_Sub4 G = 21.0, delta 0; Course151_Sub2,
//   Course152_Sub4, Course153_Sub3 G = 20.6667 (full 16:9 width), delta 0
//   small rooms (area bounds narrower than 60)  G = 15.5 (stock; huts, shops, one-screen rooms), delta 3.4444
//   wide world areas                            G = 15.75, delta 3.2778
// Cave A (0x02138800) also holds the 16:9 reach rule that used to live at 0x02138740.
// Debug words: 037D1F10/14 pipe-box markers, 037D1F18 delta bits, 037D1F1C measured area width,
// 037D1F20 camera controller pointer, 037D1F28 camera subject pointer. Area table at 02138E00.
